{title: Ivory Palaces}
{artist: Henry Barraclough}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 72}

Verse 1
My [Eb]Lord has garments [Ab]so won[Eb]drous fine, and myrrh their texture [Bb]fills;
its [Eb]fragrance reached to [Ab]this heart of [Eb]mine with [Ab]joy my [Bb]being [Eb]thrills.

Chorus
Out of the ivory [Bb]palaces, [Eb]into a world of [Ab]woe —
[Eb]only his great, e[Cm]ternal love [Ab]made my [Bb]Savior [Eb]go.
